      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name} Do you think that running `Cutout`-style alpha-clip would benefit performance at all in place of standard `<NaN, NaN, NaN>` vertex-style tile discard for android/ios devices? Also, do you think cutout style shaders would be possible to have on those platforms (for avatars), since they are rendered along opaque objects, or is the performance cost too substantial on those mobile devices for those to be an option?",
